{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZtcEos7ufA8VcpKHpVQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me understand the existing repository structure better:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-16` - Order data class currently lacks a status field\n- `OrderController.kt:21-34` - create method exists, but no cancel endpoint\n- `OrderRepository.kt` - stores orders in ConcurrentHashMap\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` - ShipmentStatus enum exists with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` - create method has no validation of order status\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` - stores shipments in ConcurrentHashMap\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` - ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) exist\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` - ErrorCode enum exists\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Errors use ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler formats them centrally\n- Controllers throw exceptions, not return error responses\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions checking both status and error envelope ($.error.code)\n- Repositories clear in-memory state with `repository.clear()` in @BeforeEach\n- Tests verify error response structure, not just status codes\n\n**Affected files and why they cannot be avoided:**\n1. `Order.kt` - must add status field to track order state\n2. `OrderController.kt` - must add cancel endpoint\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - must add method to find shipments by orderId\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` - must add check to reject shipments for cancelled orders\n5. `ApiError.kt` - may need error code for cancelled order state conflict\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - must test cancel endpoint behavior\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - must test shipment rejection for cancelled orders\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order data model change could affect JSON serialization of existing orders\n- Race conditions if checking and updating shipments in separate operations\n- Need atomic cancel operation (all-or-nothing when checking for CONFIRMED shipments)\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - the ticket clearly defines all behavior including idempotent cancels and atomic rejection when CONFIRMED shipments exist.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class, creating a new OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED states.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns immediately if order is already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - If order is ACTIVE and has a CONFIRMED shipment, throws ConflictException with 409 (atomic rejection)\n   - If order is ACTIVE with no CONFIRMED shipments, cancels it and all CREATED shipments, returns updated order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Modify create endpoint to inject OrderRepository and check if order exists and is not CANCELLED; throw ConflictException with 409 if CANCELLED.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code if needed for consistency, but the existing 409 via ConflictException is the standard.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns updated order with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 with ConflictException\n   - Cancelling non-existent order returns 404\n   - Cancelled shipments have status changed to CANCELLED\n   - Creating order returns ACTIVE status\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test for creating shipment on cancelled order returns 409.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Instead of finding shipments by orderId in the repository, we could iterate through all shipments and filter; this wastes resources and should be avoided with a dedicated query method.\n- We could use a service layer to encapsulate cancel logic; however, the existing code uses controllers directly with repositories, so we maintain that pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Cancel an ACTIVE order:*\n- Read order from repository (404 if missing)\n- Find all shipments for this order\n- Check all shipments - if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409), order stays ACTIVE\n- If all shipments are CREATED or none exist, cancel the order (status → CANCELLED)\n- For each CREATED shipment, update status to CANCELLED\n- Persist order and all modified shipments\n- Return updated order (200 OK)\n\n*Cancel an already CANCELLED order:*\n- Read order from repository (404 if missing)\n- Order is already CANCELLED, return it immediately (200 OK, idempotent)\n\n*Create shipment on CANCELLED order:*\n- Read order from repository\n- If order status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (409)\n- Otherwise, create shipment with CREATED status\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `create returns order with ACTIVE status` - verify new orders are ACTIVE\n2. `cancel ACTIVE order cancels CREATED shipments` - create order, create shipment, cancel order, verify order is CANCELLED and shipment is CANCELLED\n3. `cancel ACTIVE order with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409` - create order, create shipment, manually set to CONFIRMED (via repository), cancel order, verify 409 and nothing changed\n4. `cancel already CANCELLED order succeeds` - create order, cancel it, cancel it again, verify 200 OK\n5. `cancel non-existent order returns 404` - call cancel on missing order, verify 404\n6. `create shipment on CANCELLED order fails with 409` - create and cancel order, try to create shipment, verify 409\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1376,"cache_read_input_tokens":20812,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1376},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e4097ab-dc2d-4706-ac22-0a9b45b0b7b9","uuid":"b301a141-c24f-46fd-8dd9-4a320d0e688c","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:51:34.322Z","request_id":"req_011CfZtcERojia9WqJtebPuc"}
